This project uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB), a private EC2 instance, and a bastion instance to deploy MediaWiki as an application. The bastion instance is the only way to access the app instance through SSH, while the ALB provides public access to MediaWiki.

The security groups are not as restrictive because this is a home lab, and I cannot assign a fixed public IP address range.

CodeBuild will be used to provision the environment using Terraform. User data installs the CodeDeploy agent on the private EC2 instance, and CodeDeploy runs the `install.sh script to install and host MediaWiki.

CodeBuild has the permissions needed to create the AWS resources, although these permissions could have been more restrictive. CodeDeploy uses an AWS-managed IAM policy. The EC2 instance has the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy, which allows it to connect to AWS Systems Manager for remote management and troubleshooting without requiring SSH access.

Some mistakes have been made and i will progressively get much better.

